      "content": "a breath in the one i'm still in... but what's the point of just breathing if the air feels heavy and suffocating every single second? i look at the future and i don't see anything. i don't see a version of me that isn't a failure. it feels like i've already reached the end of my story, and now i'm just stuck in the epilogue, waiting for the lights to go out. it feels more logical to just stop fighting the inevitable than to keep dragging this shell around.",
